From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: probe -isystem with a directory in the build tree

The -isystem probe compiles with "-isystem /usr/include -Werror". A cross
compiler built with -Wpoison-system-directories rejects that directory,
so the probe fails (ISYSTEM falls back to -I) and OpenEmbedded's
configure-unsafe QA check stops the build on the error in config.log:

  cc1: error: include location "/usr/include" is unsafe for
  cross-compilation [-Werror=poison-system-directories]

The probe only asks whether the compiler takes -isystem; any directory
answers that. Use ".". configure is patched too, as it ships generated.
meta-office replaced the probe by ISYSTEM=-isystem.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -4442,7 +4442,7 @@
 if test "$GCC" = "yes"; then
     AC_MSG_CHECKING( for -isystem )
     save_CFLAGS=$CFLAGS
-    CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -isystem /usr/include -Werror"
+    CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -isystem . -Werror"
     AC_COMPILE_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([[]], [[ return 0; ]])],[ ISYSTEM="-isystem " ],[])
     CFLAGS=$save_CFLAGS
     if test -n "$ISYSTEM"; then
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -14680,7 +14680,7 @@
     { printf "%s\n" "$as_me:${as_lineno-$LINENO}: checking for -isystem " >&5
 printf %s "checking for -isystem ... " >&6; }
     save_CFLAGS=$CFLAGS
-    CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -isystem /usr/include -Werror"
+    CFLAGS="$CFLAGS -isystem . -Werror"
     cat confdefs.h - <<_ACEOF >conftest.$ac_ext
 /* end confdefs.h.  */
 
